		<range-element
			guid="86e5c062-d90f-476c-a363-264adfafedfa"
			id="7.1.9 Move a part of the body"
			parent="7.1 Posture">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving various parts of the body.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move a part of the body</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.1.9</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="c7c85346-158d-4881-839d-9a6a8e47209b"
			id="7.2 Move"
			parent="7 Physical actions">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for intransitive verbs of movement referring to moving your whole body to a different location. There are many components of meaning involved in verbs of movement. They can include a source location (from), a goal location (to), a path (along), manner (walk, run), speed (race, crawl), direction (forward, back, side, up, down, toward, away from), shape of the path (straight, curve, circle, angle), relationship to some object or objects (on, hang, against, between, across, through, into, out of, onto, off of, around), proximity (near, far), multiple movements (back and forth, return, bounce), inclusion with other objects or parts of objects (join, leave, collect, disperse, unite, separate), volition (go versus drift), intransitive versus transitive (move versus move something). Some verbs of movement do not involve moving from one place to another, but express bodily movement.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="5cc64831-c14a-4dbe-beba-214e725ad041"
			id="7.2.1 Manner of movement"
			parent="7.2 Move">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for general words referring to the way in which a person moves.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Manner of movement</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="643cc712-b3b3-42d0-971e-7a4c8a6cbf1e"
			id="7.2.1.1 Walk"
			parent="7.2.1 Manner of movement">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words related to walking--moving slowly using your legs.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Walk</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.1</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="b16de6a0-71dd-448c-9ffa-49f6646a5219"
			id="7.2.1.1.1 Run"
			parent="7.2.1.1 Walk">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to running--moving fast on your legs.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Run</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.1.1</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="a2bbf179-8d38-4d2e-84cd-0e00bb6c74f3"
			id="7.2.1.1.2 Crawl"
			parent="7.2.1.1 Walk">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to crawling--moving on your hands and knees or on your stomach.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Crawl</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.1.2</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="5abd1270-261a-4980-93e5-e10eacea99ad"
			id="7.2.1.1.3 Jump"
			parent="7.2.1.1 Walk">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to jumping--moving your body off the ground by pushing hard with your legs.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Jump</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.1.3</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="1017cbc3-0dfb-4930-9881-28f96784035c"
			id="7.2.1.2 Move quickly"
			parent="7.2.1 Manner of movement">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving quickly or slowly.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move quickly</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.2</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="e442afe1-e7cd-4ab2-b456-963e2e041a1e"
			id="7.2.1.2.1 Move slowly"
			parent="7.2.1.2 Move quickly">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving slowly.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move slowly</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.2.1</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="deff977c-a664-4456-9d44-a5127dd2a7d1"
			id="7.2.1.3 Wander"
			parent="7.2.1 Manner of movement">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to wandering--to move slowly without any purpose or goal.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Wander</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.3</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="250baab9-5a31-493c-95ea-9fee8baf9fd5"
			id="7.2.1.4 Graceful"
			parent="7.2.1 Manner of movement">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving in a graceful manner.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Graceful</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.4</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="b5aa5873-4c66-4d2d-935a-18e0ab231dbb"
			id="7.2.1.4.1 Clumsy"
			parent="7.2.1.4 Graceful">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving in a clumsy manner.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Clumsy</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.4.1</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="879e66bc-af29-4fe4-86e0-0047973a57d6"
			id="7.2.1.5 Walk with difficulty"
			parent="7.2.1 Manner of movement">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to walking with some difficulty such as stumbling--to miss your step because of hitting an object such as a stone, hole, or mud; staggering--to walk unsteadily because of weakness, illness, or drunkenness; or limping--to walk unevenly or with difficulty because of injury to a foot.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Walk with difficulty</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.5</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="3f535689-944a-4e9c-8f64-ec6395b7c8d7"
			id="7.2.1.5.1 Slip, slide"
			parent="7.2.1.5 Walk with difficulty">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for moving across a smooth or lubricated surface.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Slip, slide</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.5.1</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="985f099d-f38c-4957-907a-769d1a45ca10"
			id="7.2.1.6 Steady, unsteady"
			parent="7.2.1 Manner of movement">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words that refer to balancing yourself or something--when someone or something is able stand or move without falling.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Steady, unsteady</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.6</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="c6132280-d2aa-46f8-9e94-b087dbda09cb"
			id="7.2.1.6.1 Balance"
			parent="7.2.1.6 Steady, unsteady">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words that refer to balancing yourself or something--when someone or something is able stand or move without falling.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Balance</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.6.1</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="32d5b3de-0500-4ad6-b94e-20b8001d0a91"
			id="7.2.1.7 Move noisily"
			parent="7.2.1 Manner of movement">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to making a noise while moving.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move noisily</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.1.7</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="12fe5f6c-7f98-47ba-936a-bcd1065c2db3"
			id="7.2.2 Move in a direction"
			parent="7.2 Move">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use the domains in this section for words referring to moving in a direction related to the orientation of the person's body (not in relation to the position of the destination).</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move in a direction</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.2</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="8e59041e-660b-4f3e-9a11-83217417209e"
			id="7.2.2.1 Move forward"
			parent="7.2.2 Move in a direction">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving in a forward direction--in the same direction the person is facing.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move forward</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.2.1</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="6de4e99b-2b5a-493a-a208-f024d1eabdf3"
			id="7.2.2.2 Move back"
			parent="7.2.2 Move in a direction">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving in a backward direction--the person is facing one direction, but moving toward their back--to move in the opposite direction from the direction the person is facing.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move back</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.2.2</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="f4b18e9c-b465-4763-ba79-d7eed2cebcfa"
			id="7.2.2.3 Move sideways"
			parent="7.2.2 Move in a direction">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving in a sideways direction--the person is facing one direction, but moving toward their side.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move sideways</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.2.3</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="9d6cbe74-93d6-41fb-b7e2-cc30adb28187"
			id="7.2.2.4 Move up"
			parent="7.2.2 Move in a direction">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving in an upward direction or to moving to a higher place.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move up</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.2.4</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="16081dd6-72e5-4826-b86d-958dd82a01c0"
			id="7.2.2.5 Move down"
			parent="7.2.2 Move in a direction">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving in a downward direction or to moving to a lower place.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move down</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.2.5</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="b14db9f4-5e1d-4a2b-bec0-0d6bcb5b1a31"
			id="7.2.2.5.1 Fall"
			parent="7.2.2.5 Move down">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to something falling--for something to move down under the influence of gravity.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Fall</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.2.5.1</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="60a5fa58-45b1-41ae-9430-5200e8bfbcb8"
			id="7.2.2.6 Turn"
			parent="7.2.2 Move in a direction">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to turning and changing the direction in which one is moving.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Turn</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.2.6</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="8bcc3b3d-dd0c-4838-a33a-b395f354c86f"
			id="7.2.2.7 Move in a circle"
			parent="7.2.2 Move in a direction">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to continually changing the direction you are facing in until you are once again facing in the same direction, e.g. moving in a circle, moving around something, or rotating.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move in a circle</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.2.7</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="3c9fe647-2647-4f43-8bac-7facc054f7ff"
			id="7.2.2.8 Move back and forth"
			parent="7.2.2 Move in a direction">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words related to moving back and forth.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move back and forth</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.2.8</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="36176d59-171b-4a0a-a0f7-a8f9857536a1"
			id="7.2.2.9 Move straight without turning"
			parent="7.2.2 Move in a direction">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving straight without changing direction.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move straight without turning</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.2.9</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="fcd22c85-7ee1-4d31-8633-9dbd32344211"
			id="7.2.3 Move toward something"
			parent="7.2 Move">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving toward, in the direction of, or near something or some place. The words in this domain should refer to moving in the direction of a place, but should not require that the person actually arrived. Some languages (such as German and Polish) distinguish 'go on foot' from 'go in a vehicle'.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move toward something</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.3</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="5832eb32-8a90-42a7-b2bc-a9bb575b1b7c"
			id="7.2.3.1 Move away"
			parent="7.2.3 Move toward something">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving away from a place.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Move away</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.3.1</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="2cc624fa-76cb-46ab-87c8-c13c6adb1c72"
			id="7.2.3.2 Go"
			parent="7.2.3 Move toward something">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving away from the speaker. In Australian languages many movement words are marked for direction toward or away from the speaker.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Go</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.3.2</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="aa8d812b-7c13-414a-ad02-a4240d2cef68"
			id="7.2.3.2.1 Come"
			parent="7.2.3.2 Go">
			<description>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Use this domain for words referring to moving toward the speaker.</text>
				</form>
			</description>
			<label>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>Come</text>
				</form>
			</label>
			<abbrev>
				<form
					lang="en">
					<text>7.2.3.2.1</text>
				</form>
			</abbrev>
		</range-element>
		<range-element
			guid="20e7d987-0d55-46d4-ab69-0b0cce2f1e24"
			id="7.2.3.3 Leave"
			parent="7.2.3 Move toward something">
			<description>
				<form
